-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: as in coa9-strategic.l4 (JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the text says no in its own words or a
-- fork-register choice applies; NOTHING where the text does not decide). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Section 417 is blank in this text. Section 416(1)(b) and (2) are blank. Section 416(4) is a regulation-making power.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 415: Duty to prepare directors' report
-- =========================================================================================================

§ `s 415 Duty to prepare directors' report`

-- src:5552 | 415 Duty to prepare directors' report
-- src:5553 | (1) The directors of a company must prepare a directors' report for each financial year of the company.
@ref s 415(1) The directors must prepare a directors' report for each financial year (src:5552-5553)
GIVEN `the directors have prepared a directors' report for the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 415(1) the directors have prepared the directors' report for the financial year` MEANS
    IF `the directors have prepared a directors' report for the financial year`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a bare "must" not met, decided case by case, fork F11): "The directors of a company must prepare a directors' report for each financial year of the company."

-- src:5554 | (1A) Subsection (1) does not apply if the company qualifies as a micro-entity (see sections 384A and 384B).
@ref s 415(1A) Subsection (1) does not apply to a micro-entity (src:5554)
GIVEN `s 384A the company qualifies as a micro-entity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 415(1A) subsection (1) does not apply to the company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 384A the company qualifies as a micro-entity`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", reading (a) for a lawyer): "Subsection (1) does not apply if the company qualifies as a micro-entity"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company qualifies as a micro-entity is decided by sections 384A and 384B

-- src:5555 | (2) For a financial year in which—
-- src:5556 | (a) the company is a parent company, and
-- src:5557 | (b) the directors of the company prepare group accounts,
-- src:5558 | the directors' report must be a consolidated report (a “group directors' report”) relating to the undertakings included in the consolidation.
@ref s 415(2) A parent company that prepares group accounts must prepare a consolidated directors' report (src:5555-5558)
-- SEAM (PLAN 4.1): section 1173(1). The caller answers it for the financial year in question ("For a financial year in which the company is a parent company").
GIVEN `s 1173(1) the company is a parent company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the directors of the company prepare group accounts for the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 415(2) the directors' report must be a consolidated report` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the directors of the company prepare group accounts for the financial year`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a "where" condition that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b); fork F33): "For a financial year in which— ... (b) the directors of the company prepare group accounts"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1173(1) the company is a parent company`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a "where" condition that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b); fork F33): "For a financial year in which— (a) the company is a parent company"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a parent company is decided by section 1173(1)

@ref s 415(2) (src:5555)
GIVEN `the report is a consolidated report relating to the undertakings included in the consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 415(2) the report is a group directors' report` MEANS
    IF `the report is a consolidated report relating to the undertakings included in the consolidation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a consolidated report (a “group directors' report”) relating to the undertakings included in the consolidation"

-- src:5559 | (3) A group directors' report may, where appropriate, give greater emphasis to the matters that are significant to the undertakings included in the consolidation, taken as a whole.
@ref s 415(3) A group directors' report may give greater emphasis to matters significant to the group (src:5559)
GIVEN `the report is a group directors' report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is appropriate to give greater emphasis to the matters that are significant to the undertakings included in the consolidation, taken as a whole` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 415(3) the group directors' report may give greater emphasis to the matters significant to the undertakings included in the consolidation` MEANS
    IF `the report is a group directors' report`
       AND `it is appropriate to give greater emphasis to the matters that are significant to the undertakings included in the consolidation, taken as a whole`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A group directors' report may, where appropriate, give greater emphasis"; the permission does not forbid anything else

-- src:5560 | (4) In the case of failure to comply with the requirement to prepare a directors' report, an offence is committed by every person who—
-- src:5561 | (a) was a director of the company immediately before the end of the period for filing accounts and reports for the financial year in question, and
-- src:5562 | (b) failed to take all reasonable steps for securing compliance with that requirement.
@ref s 415(4) A director commits an offence if no directors' report is prepared (src:5560-5562)
GIVEN `the company has failed to comply with the requirement to prepare a directors' report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was a director of the company immediately before the end of the period for filing accounts and reports for the financial year in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person failed to take all reasonable steps for securing compliance with that requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 415(4) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company has failed to comply with the requirement to prepare a directors' report`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind ("In the case of" read like "where", ruling of 2026-11-05 (b), fork F12): "In the case of failure to comply with the requirement to prepare a directors' report, an offence is committed"
    ELSE IF `the person was a director of the company immediately before the end of the period for filing accounts and reports for the financial year in question`
            AND `the person failed to take all reasonable steps for securing compliance with that requirement`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence is committed by every person who— (a) was a director of the company immediately before the end of the period for filing accounts and reports ..., and (b) failed to take all reasonable steps"

-- src:5563 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:5564 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:5565 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 415(5) Penalty for an offence under section 415 (src:5563-5565)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 415(5) the penalty for an offence under section 415` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection distinguishes conviction on indictment from summary conviction and does not distinguish the parts of the United Kingdom

