§ `s 415A Directors' report: small companies exemption`

-- src:5566 | 415A Directors' report: small companies exemption
-- src:5567 | (1) A company is entitled to small companies exemption in relation to the directors' report for a financial year if—
-- src:5568 | (a) it is entitled to prepare accounts for the year in accordance with the small companies regime, or
-- src:5569 | (b) it would be so entitled but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group.
@ref s 415A(1) Entitlement to small companies exemption (src:5566-5569)
GIVEN `s 381 the company is entitled to prepare accounts for the year in accordance with the small companies regime` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company would be so entitled but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 415A(1) the company is entitled to small companies exemption in relation to the directors' report` MEANS
    IF `s 381 the company is entitled to prepare accounts for the year in accordance with the small companies regime` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `the company would be so entitled but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `s 381 the company is entitled to prepare accounts for the year in accordance with the small companies regime` EQUALS NOTHING
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): entitlement to the small companies regime is decided by sections 381 to 384
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is entitled to small companies exemption in relation to the directors' report for a financial year if— (a) ..., or (b) ..."

