-- src:5597 | (5) Where a directors' report containing the statement required by this section is approved but the statement is false, every director of the company who—
-- src:5598 | (a) knew that the statement was false, or was reckless as to whether it was false, and
-- src:5599 | (b) failed to take reasonable steps to prevent the report from being approved,
-- src:5600 | commits an offence.
@ref s 418(5) A director who knowingly or recklessly lets a false statement be approved commits an offence (src:5597-5600)
GIVEN `a directors' report containing the statement required by this section is approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is false` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director knew that the statement was false` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director was reckless as to whether the statement was false` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director failed to take reasonable steps to prevent the report from being approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 418(5) the director commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`a directors' report containing the statement required by this section is approved` AND `the statement is false`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a "where" condition that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)): "Where a directors' report containing the statement required by this section is approved but the statement is false"
    ELSE IF `the person is a director of the company`
            AND (`the director knew that the statement was false` OR `the director was reckless as to whether the statement was false`)
            AND `the director failed to take reasonable steps to prevent the report from being approved`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every director of the company who— (a) knew that the statement was false, or was reckless as to whether it was false, and (b) failed to take reasonable steps to prevent the report from being approved"

-- src:5601 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (5) is liable—
-- src:5602 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
-- src:5603 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:5604 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding twelve months or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both);
-- src:5605 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months, or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
@ref s 418(6) Penalty for an offence under section 418(5) (src:5601-5605)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 418(6) the penalty for an offence under section 418(5)` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, JUST (Period OF 2, Years), JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, JUST (Period OF 12, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): summary conviction is divided by place, and a summary conviction that does not say where is not provided for

